#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:2
msgid "CyberArk Conjur"
msgstr "CyberArk Conjur"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:4
msgid ""
"|morpheus| supports integration with CyberArk Conjur for stored credential "
"sets as well utilization of Conjur-stored secret values via |morpheus| "
"Cypher service. This works identically to built-in credential storage and "
"built-in Cypher functionality with the exception that your Conjur server is "
"the storage backend rather than the |morpheus| appliance itself. In some "
"cases, this may help to consolidate secret management into one central place"
" or it even may be a requirement to satisfy internal security policies at "
"some organizations."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| supports integration con CyberArk Conjur para stored credential "
"sets as well utilization of Conjur-stored secret valores via |morpheus| "
"Cypher servicio. This works identically to built-in credential storage y "
"built-in Cypher functionality con el exception que your Conjur server es el "
"storage backend rather than el |morpheus| appliance itself. In algunos "
"cases, este puede help to consolidate secret management en one central place"
" o it incluso puede be un requirement to satisfy interno security policies "
"at algunos organizations."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:6
msgid ""
"CyberArk Conjur integration is not included with |morpheus| out of the box. "
"It is developed as an official plugin and may be applied to any |morpheus| "
"appliance that needs it. See the |morpheus| plugin repository website for "
"access to the latest version of the plugin."
msgstr ""
"CyberArk Conjur integration no es incluido con |morpheus| out of el box. It "
"es developed as un official plugin y puede be applied to cualquier "
"|morpheus| appliance que needs it. See el |morpheus| plugin repository "
"website para acceso to el latest versión of el plugin."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:9
msgid "Applying the Plugin"
msgstr "Applying el Plugin"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:11
msgid ""
"The latest version of the CyberArk Conjur plugin is available at the "
"|morpheus| `plugin share site <https://share.morpheusdata.com/>`_. Select "
"the pane for the correct plugin and click the :guilabel:`DOWNLOAD` button. "
"The plugin JAR file will be downloaded to the local computer you're working "
"on."
msgstr ""
"The latest versión of el CyberArk Conjur plugin es disponible at el "
"|morpheus| `plugin share site <https://share.morpheusdata.com/>`_. "
"Seleccione el pane para el correct plugin y click el :guilabel:`DOWNLOAD` "
"botón. The plugin JAR archivo será be downloaded to el local computer you're"
" working on."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:14
msgid ".. image:: images/integration_guides/conjur/share.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/integration_guides/conjur/share.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:15
msgid ""
"With the plugin downloaded, head back to |morpheus| to apply the plugin to "
"your appliance. Plugins are added by navigating to |AdmIntPlu| and clicking "
":guilabel:`ADD`. Drop the plugin JAR file onto the target and click "
":guilabel:`UPLOAD`. It may take a few moments for the plugin to be applied "
"successfully and for the modal to be dismissed after clicking the upload "
"button."
msgstr ""
"With el plugin downloaded, head back to |morpheus| to apply el plugin to "
"your appliance. Plugins son agregado by navigating to |AdmIntPlu| y clicking"
" :guilabel:`AGREGAR`. Drop el plugin JAR archivo sobre el destino y click "
":guilabel:`UPLOAD`. It puede take un few moments para el plugin to be "
"applied successfully y para el modal to be dismissed después de clicking el "
"upload botón."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:18
msgid ".. image:: images/integration_guides/conjur/addPlugin.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/integration_guides/conjur/addPlugin.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:19
msgid ""
"Once the plugin is added, we configure the connection details here. Edit the"
" new Conjur plugin by clicking the pencil (|pencil|) icon from its row in "
"the list. Configure the following fields:"
msgstr ""
"Once el plugin es agregado, we configure el conexión detalles aquí. Edit el "
"nuevo Conjur plugin by clicking el pencil (|pencil|) icon desde its row in "
"el lista. Configure los siguientes campos:"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:21
msgid ""
"**NAME:** A friendly name for the new integration to identify it within "
"|morpheus|"
msgstr ""
"**NAME:** A friendly nombre para el nuevo integration to identify it dentro "
"de |morpheus|"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:22
msgid ""
"**ENABLED:** Mark the box to make this integration active and available"
msgstr "**ENABLED:** Mark el box to make esta integración activo y disponible"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:23
msgid ""
"**CONJUR API URL:** The full URL for the Conjur server, usually listening on"
" port 8443"
msgstr ""
"**CONJUR API URL:** The full URL para el Conjur server, usually listening on"
" puerto 8443"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:24
msgid ""
"**CONJUR USERNAME:** The Conjur user account you wish to authenticate with. "
"This user should have read, write, and execute access to the variables "
"configured within the Conjur policy"
msgstr ""
"**CONJUR USERNAME:** The Conjur user cuenta you wish to authenticate con. "
"This user debería tienen read, write, y execute acceso to el variables "
"configurado dentro de el Conjur policy"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:25
msgid ""
"**CONJUR USERNAME API KEY:** The API key for user entered in the prior field"
msgstr ""
"**CONJUR USERNAME API KEY:** The API key para user entered in el prior campo"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:26
msgid ""
"**CONJUR ORGANIZATION:** The Conjur account in which the user and variables "
"reside"
msgstr ""
"**CONJUR ORGANIZATION:** The Conjur cuenta in cual el usuario y variables "
"reside"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:27
msgid ""
"**CLEAR SECRET ON DELETION:** When marked, secret values will be cleared "
"when deleted from |morpheus|"
msgstr ""
"**CLEAR SECRET ON DELETION:** When marked, secret valores será be cleared "
"cuando eliminado desde |morpheus|"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:29
msgid ""
"Variables are predefined by Conjur policies. This integration does not allow"
" users to create variables but does allow you to read and update their "
"values. If the plugin is configured to clear secrets that are deleted from "
"|morpheus|, the variable value is updated with an empty value as there is no"
" concept of fully deleting secrets in the Conjur API. If the plugin is "
"configured not to clear secrets on deletion, the secret object is deleted "
"from |morpheus| without altering it on the Conjur backend."
msgstr ""
"Variables son predefined by Conjur policies. Esta integración no allow users"
" to create variables pero does allow you to read y update their valores. If "
"el plugin es configurado to clear secrets que son eliminado desde "
"|morpheus|, el variable valor es actualizado con un vacío valor as allí es "
"no concept of fully deleting secrets in el Conjur API. If el plugin es "
"configurado no to clear secrets on deletion, el secret objeto es eliminado "
"desde |morpheus| sin altering it on el Conjur backend."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:31
msgid ""
"By applying and configuring the plugin, the appliance now has the "
"Conjur/Cypher integration available. If you don't intend to use the "
"credential store integration, you can stop here and look ahead to the "
"feature demonstration further ahead in this guide. If you do intend to use "
"the credential store integration as well, there's one additional "
"configuration step to take in the next section."
msgstr ""
"By applying y configuring el plugin, el appliance ahora tiene el "
"Conjur/Cypher integration disponible. If you don't intend to use el "
"credential store integration, you puede stop aquí y look ahead to el "
"característica demonstration further ahead en esta guía. If you do intend to"
" use el credential store integration as well, allí's one adicional "
"configuración paso to take in el siguiente sección."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:34
msgid "Adding A Conjur Trust Integration"
msgstr "Agregar A Conjur Trust integración"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:36
msgid ""
"In order to use Conjur with |morpheus| credentials, we must also add a "
"Conjur-type integration in |InfTruInt|. By applying the plugin in the "
"previous step, we now have the ability to add this type of integration. From"
" the Trust integrations list page, click :guilabel:`+ ADD` and select "
"\"Conjur.\" It's important to note that you **do not** need to again "
"configure the API URL and Conjur login credentials as we just did in the "
"previous step. You may configure them here if you wish, such as if you were "
"making multiple integrations with multiple Conjur appliances, but if you're "
"simply integrating with the same appliance and user account, this is "
"unnecessary. Simply give the new Trust integration a friendly name for "
"reference in |morpheus| and indicate the desired mount point for secrets you"
" wish to consume as done in the screenshot below."
msgstr ""
"In order to use Conjur con |morpheus| credentials, we debe también add un "
"Conjur-tipo integration in |InfTruInt|. By applying el plugin in el anterior"
" paso, we ahora tienen el ability to add este tipo of integration. Desde el "
"Trust integrations página de lista, click :guilabel:`+ AGREGAR` y select "
"\"Conjur.\" It's importante to tenga en cuenta que you **no** need to again "
"configure el API URL y Conjur login credentials as we solo did in el "
"anterior paso. You puede configure them aquí if you wish, como if you fueron"
" making múltiples integrations con múltiples Conjur appliances, pero if "
"you're simply integrating con el mismo appliance y user cuenta, este es "
"unnecessary. Simply give el nuevo Trust integration un friendly nombre para "
"referencia in |morpheus| y indicate el desired mount point para secrets you "
"wish to consume as done in el screenshot a continuación."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:38
msgid ""
"In many cases, you don't have to configure the connection details when "
"adding a Conjur Trust integration. See the paragraph above."
msgstr ""
"In muchos cases, you don't tienen to configure el conexión detalles cuando "
"adding un Conjur Trust integration. See el paragraph anterior."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:41
msgid ".. image:: images/integration_guides/conjur/addTrustInt.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/integration_guides/conjur/addTrustInt.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:43
msgid "Conjur and Credential Stores"
msgstr "Conjur y Credential Stores"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:45
msgid ""
"With configurations completed, we can take a look at how |morpheus| is able "
"to interface with Conjur as a credential store. As mentioned at the "
"beginning of this guide, variables are created by Conjur policies and not by"
" |morpheus|. We can reference existing variables and update the secret "
"values stored within."
msgstr ""
"With configurations completed, we puede take un look at how |morpheus| es "
"capaz de interfaz con Conjur as un credential store. As mentioned at el "
"beginning of este guía, variables son creado by Conjur policies y no by "
"|morpheus|. We puede referencia existente variables y update el secret "
"valores stored dentro de."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:47
msgid ""
"As an example, there is a variable named ``BotApp/secretVar`` in the target "
"Conjur appliance. When configuring the Trust integration (in the prior "
"section), the ``BotApp/`` mount point was referenced (see the screenshot in "
"the last section). When creating stored credential sets in |morpheus| "
"against this Conjur credential store, reference the rest of the variable "
"path as the NAME value on the credential set. In this case, the credential "
"set will be named ``secretVar`` to complete the ``BotApp/secretVar`` path as"
" shown in the screenshot below. Be sure to also select Conjur as the "
"CREDENTIAL STORE value rather than the default \"Internal.\""
msgstr ""
"As un ejemplo, allí es un variable named ``BotApp/secretVar`` in el destino "
"Conjur appliance. When configuring el Trust integration (in el prior "
"sección), el ``BotApp/`` mount point fue referenced (see el screenshot in el"
" último sección). When creating stored credential sets in |morpheus| against"
" este Conjur credential store, referencia el rest of el variable ruta as el "
"NAME valor on el credential set. In este case, el credential set será be "
"named ``secretVar`` to completo el ``BotApp/secretVar`` ruta como se muestra"
" en el screenshot a continuación. Be sure to también select Conjur as el "
"CREDENTIAL STORE valor rather than el predeterminado \"Internal.\""

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:50
msgid ".. image:: images/integration_guides/conjur/credentials.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/integration_guides/conjur/credentials.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:51
msgid ""
"After saving and going back to the Conjur appliance, the value stored at the"
" referenced variable has been updated. This credential set is also available"
" for use anywhere |morpheus| allows users to utilize them, such as when "
"integrating new Clouds, authenticating REST calls to populate Option Lists, "
"and many other places."
msgstr ""
"After saving y going back to el Conjur appliance, el valor stored at el "
"referenced variable tiene sido actualizado. This credential set es también "
"disponible para use anywhere |morpheus| permite un los usuarios utilize "
"them, como cuando integrating nuevo Clouds, authenticating REST calls to "
"populate Option Lists, y muchos otro places."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:54
msgid "Conjur and Cypher"
msgstr "Conjur y Cypher"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:56
msgid ""
"In addition to stored credential sets, the CyberArk Conjur plugin also "
"enables integration with |morpheus| Cypher. Just as calls can be made to "
"internally-stored secret values with Cypher, Conjur variable endpoints may "
"be referenced to onboard secret strings into automation Tasks."
msgstr ""
"Además to stored credential sets, el CyberArk Conjur plugin también enables "
"integration con |morpheus| Cypher. Just as calls puede be made to "
"internally-stored secret valores con Cypher, Conjur variable endpoints puede"
" be referenced to onboard secret strings en automation Tasks."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:58
msgid ""
"In the screenshot below, see a simple shell script Task which echoes out a "
"secret value stored in Conjur. As you can see, the ``conjur/`` mount point "
"is referenced along with the rest of the path to the variable which should "
"be accessed. After executing the Task, we can check the execution history "
"and see that the Conjur-stored value is indeed echoed back out."
msgstr ""
"En el screenshot a continuación, see un simple shell script Task cual echoes"
" out un secret valor stored in Conjur. As you puede see, el ``conjur/`` "
"mount point es referenced junto con el rest of el ruta to el variable cual "
"debería be accessed. After executing el Task, we puede check el execution "
"history y see que el Conjur-stored valor es indeed echoed back out."

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:61
msgid ".. image:: images/integration_guides/conjur/cypherTask.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/integration_guides/conjur/cypherTask.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/trust/conjur.rst:62
msgid ""
"If desired, the value stored in Conjur could also be updated through the "
"|morpheus| Cypher UI. Navigate to |TooCyp| and click :guilabel:`+ ADD`. Note"
" the ``conjur`` mount point is included in the example list of available "
"mount points shown in the modal. By creating a new Cypher entry at the "
"``conjur`` mount point which references an existing Conjur variable path, "
"the value in Conjur can be overwritten. If you've configured the plugin to "
"clear secrets on deletion, you can also update the stored value with an "
"empty string when you delete the Cypher object in |morpheus|. For our "
"example case, we could update the value in Conjur by creating a Cypher entry"
" at the mount point ``conjur/BotApp/secretVar``."
msgstr ""
"If desired, el valor stored in Conjur podría también be actualizado a través"
" de el |morpheus| Cypher UI. Navegue un |TooCyp| y click :guilabel:`+ "
"AGREGAR`. Note el ``conjur`` mount point es incluido in el ejemplo lista of "
"disponible mount points shown in el modal. By creating un nuevo Cypher entry"
" at el ``conjur`` mount point cual references un existente Conjur variable "
"ruta, el valor in Conjur puede be overwritten. If you've configurado el "
"plugin to clear secrets on deletion, you puede también update el stored "
"valor con un vacío string cuando you delete el Cypher objeto in |morpheus|. "
"For our ejemplo case, we podría update el valor in Conjur by creating un "
"Cypher entry at el mount point ``conjur/BotApp/secretVar``."

